    "content_1": "4",
    "overall_1": "6",
    "detailed_feedback_1": "I saw blue rectangles rapidly moving toward me. I also at times saw everything become all white. So the light moving toward and the red white and blue colors are pretty accurate, except when I saw white I only saw white with circles with no other colors, and when I saw the blue rectangles it was against an all red background. The part of the picture with the desks in the room with the windows was not part of my experience at all, just the colors and the shapes of this image.",
    "final_image_2": "7000_dalle_3",
    "color_2": "9",
    "shape_2": "3",
    "content_2": "5",
    "overall_2": "6",
    "detailed_feedback_2": "The light coming towards me well represents what I saw. At one time my vision was all red and then the rectangle like in the center of this image appeared and bigger ones appeared as they got closer and closer. When I saw the rectangles I only saw them against a ared background with no white, but at a different time I did see white. I never saw an outline of a white square. What happened instead is that the border of the red screen blurred and my whole vision became red. This image also depicts light shown in rays, but I did not experience that, rather it was just blurs of color, except for the vivid shape of the blue rectangles and black rings.",
    "final_image_3": "7000_stable_2",
    "color_3": "8",
    "shape_3": "8",
    "content_3": "9",
    "overall_3": "8",
    "detailed_feedback_3": "This one is very accurate with the red color blurring and expanding beyond the screen to take up most of the visual field. This is what I experienced. Also, the white is accurate because at times the red that had blurred together turned into white. Finally, the black circles are mostly accurate because when the blurred red turned to all white, I saw black circles on only the top left of my vision, and they were more like rings because they were not filled in circles."
